  "planned_design": {
    "simulators": ["dyngen", "scmultisim", "sergio", "boolode", "genespider2"],
    "replicates_per_condition": 5,
    "regimes": ["group_only", "order_aware"],
    "factors": [
      "topology",
      "core_panel_size_variation",
      "kinetics_noise",
      "technical_noise",
      "dropout",
      "population_imbalance_and_small_groups",
      "dynamic_rewiring",
      "invariant_network_control"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Full is the frozen publication budget and contains 60 held-out datasets: 40 with dynamic group-specific truth and 20 invariant-network controls.",
      "The confirmatory family uses four dyngen and four scMultiSim conditions, giving each simulator 20 independent blocks; AUPR on directed edges is primary and AUROC is secondary.",
      "The medium scMultiSim block reaches 400 genes, 100 candidate regulators and 600-800 cells so external accuracy is not inferred only from 70-80-gene systems.",
      "Invariant controls quantify spurious group-to-group reconfiguration in a dedicated exploratory endpoint and never enter the confirmatory accuracy ranking.",
      "Simulator-derived group order is evaluated only as an explicitly labelled oracle-information sensitivity because it provides information unavailable to SPATHI; this upper-bound stratum never enters the primary ranking.",
      "No run receives a truth-derived regulatory prior or target list.",
      "Each independently simulated dataset contributes one equally weighted paired block. Conclusions therefore target this explicitly declared condition panel rather than a hypothetical equally weighted population of simulators.",
      "All full-test generation seeds come from the full.test namespace in experiments/v1/seeds/seed-plan.json and are disjoint from reduced, development, validation and all other protected namespaces.",
      "The statistical stream root for this profile is seed.full.test.statistical (1698096914).",
      "Predeclared failure policy: a configuration is excluded from a paired comparison if any required block fails; failures, timeouts and resource-limit events remain reported and no failed block is silently imputed."
    ]
  },
